Subject: [PATCH 13/13] arm64: dts: apple: t6050-j714s: Show the software camera
 indicator (slot 3)

The J714s camera light stays off: upstream replaced the light with a
software indicator the DCP draws while the camera streams (#2561), which a
board opts into. DRM owns swap slots 0 and 1 on the J714s DCP (no
apple,iomfb-surfaces), so the indicator takes slot 3, as on J615.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s.dts
@@ -1123,3 +1123,17 @@
 
 /* HDMI, through ATC3 and the on-board DP-to-HDMI converter */
 #include "t6050-j714s-hdmi.dtsi"
+
+/*
+ * The camera has no light the kernel drives here; the DCP draws upstream's software indicator
+ * (#2561) while the camera streams. DRM owns swap slots 0 and 1 on this DCP (no
+ * apple,iomfb-surfaces), so the indicator takes slot 3, as on J615: in slot 2 it would only
+ * show where the desktop is transparent.
+ */
+&dcp {
+	apple,camera-indicator-surface = <3>;
+};
+
+&isp0 {
+	apple,camera-indicator = <&dcp>;
+};
